{"item": "F-0164", "job": "adjudicate-f-0164", "kind": "ruling", "product": "asf", "text": "Disputed: whether F-0164's \"NO STORIES -> SPEC-AMEND\" stalemate (3 sessions, none closing it) was a content disagreement or a structural one a 4th attempt would also hit. Checked in the checkout, not reasoned: the spec's stories: (docs/specs/f-0164.md) named three Stories — S-39700, S-39701, S-39702 — for three Tasks, but docs/plans/replans/f-0164-cdcfd081dba8.md, landed in the same commit as the spec and plan, had already cut the live plan to one Task (T-0756, S-39702 only) and recorded why (the 240 s stray-branch cost is what gets fixed; the measurement and the timeout-park do not) — and already recommended spinning S-39700 and S-39701 off as a Feature and a Bug. A spec-amend session told to derive Stories from \"the Feature's spec, plan and landed Tasks\" (asf/feeder/rows.py:425-427) had two sources that disagreed on the count, and that contradiction, not the design, is what three sessions could not close — a fourth would hit the same wall. Upheld: the spec now follows the already-approved replan. stories: names S-39702 alone; the ## Stories list strikes S-39700 and S-39701 as cut, pointing at the replan, with their design (## The design §§1-4, now docs/specs/f-0164.md:166-328) left intact and unlabelled as waste, exactly as the replan called it — reusable verbatim by whichever new card inherits it. T-0756's own design, writes and acceptance are untouched.", "ts": "2026-10-07T00:12:43Z"}
